# BUG: comparing two & values crashes the interpreter.
#
# Expected:  either a Type error (if & values cannot be compared) or a Bool
# Actual:    Fatal error: exception File "src/line_mix/interpret.ml", line 81, characters 9-15: Assertion failed
#
# Where: interpret.ml, `equal_value` has no case for VWith, so it reaches `| _ -> assert false`.
# Decide: should & be comparable? A VWith holds unevaluated expressions, so probably not.
#         Then the type checker (`Equal` in infer) should reject it.

(1 & 2) = (1 & 2);
